Package: esidx
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34)
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: ext4 search index engine with an Everything (ETP) server
 esidx walks a directory tree into a snapshot, answers Everything's search language
 (ext:, dc:, dm:, size:, parent:, path:, wildcards, boolean and grouping) over the ETP
 protocol, and reconciles that snapshot from kernel filesystem events so it stays current
 without a periodic rescan.
 .
 The event source is a separate privileged process (sfa-server): it holds CAP_SYS_ADMIN
 because fanotify does, and hands absolute paths over a group-owned socket to an index
 server that holds no capabilities at all. The split is enforced by the systemd units this
 package installs, not by a promise in a comment.
 .
 This package installs two systemd units and the configuration they read
 (/etc/default/esidx). It enables them but does not start them: the index server needs a
 snapshot, and building the first one scans the tree, which does not belong in a package
 maintainer script. The install output says the two commands.
